{
	title: 'Background bash: result arrives as a message',
	spec: "The bash tool takes an optional background: true (questions.md item 29). The command starts at once in its own process group; the call waits at most 100 ms, so a command that fails at once (not found, syntax error, exit within 100 ms) returns its output and exit code as a normal result; otherwise it returns 'started in background as <id>' and the turn goes on. When the command exits, its output (capped and saved like a normal bash result) and exit code reach the session as an advisory message from 'bash <id>', delivered like messages from other sessions (task rj): into the running turn at the next tool result, or starting a turn when the session is idle, except while the user has it paused. Escape does not kill background commands; closing the session or quitting the last Hal process does, as for foreground ones. Background commands survive neither a host restart nor a takeover: after one, the session gets 'bash <id> was lost when Hal restarted'.",
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['1r', 'rj'],
	foldInto: ['1r'],
	notes: [
		'Process running for both modes lives in src/host/jobs.ts (exec, plus the background registry); tools/bash.ts only validates and picks a mode. tools.cap is the shared output cut, so the delivered message is capped like a result.',
		"The message is prompts.submit with Sender { from: <the session itself>, label: 'bash <id>', advisory: true }; from set means it waits while paused/failed and never promotes a subagent. subagents.owed treats from === self like a subagent's report: the turn it starts inherits who owns the work.",
		"Background calls get no default timeout (only an explicit one) and ignore the turn's abort signal, including during the 100 ms grace wait.",
		"Running ids are kept in session.ason `background` (validated as a list of strings). host.init's exit handler (and host.reset) calls jobs.killAll without clearing it, so main.becomeHost's jobs.lost() finds the ids of open tabs and busy sessions and sends 'bash <id> was lost when Hal restarted'. Tab close (tabs.close) kills silently and clears it; closing a tab never stopped foreground turns, so this is the only kill on close.",
		"subagents.finished does not close a subagent's tab while it has background commands, since closing would kill them."
	]
}
